The preserved original default profile is from github.com/moby/profiles/seccomp
v0.2.3, commit 836ae4d37ef2ec995c77c99fc55f5b5f3af3a897. Docker Engine
29.5.2 commit 568f755ebeb1ac9c6a8febbda6cd371ea0a9630b pins this module.
The corresponding Apache license is preserved in tool-os-krb5-seccomp.LICENSE.

Local modification, 16 November 2026: tool-os-krb5-seccomp.json preserves every
original profile rule and appends one allow rule for add_key, keyctl and
request_key. It is used only by the isolated Kerberos ordinary-test builder.
Tests use an exclusive nonroot UID, zero capabilities and private keyrings.
Kernel keyrings are not namespaced. No global policy is changed.

Sources:
https://github.com/moby/profiles/blob/836ae4d37ef2ec995c77c99fc55f5b5f3af3a897/seccomp/default.json
https://github.com/moby/profiles/blob/836ae4d37ef2ec995c77c99fc55f5b5f3af3a897/seccomp/default_linux.go
https://github.com/moby/moby/blob/568f755ebeb1ac9c6a8febbda6cd371ea0a9630b/go.mod
https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/seccomp/
